/* FreeSpaceKit */
"Wipe Free Space" = "擦除空闲空间";
"Volume" = "宗卷";
"Target" = "目标";
"Free now" = "当前空闲空间";
"Rescan Volumes" = "重新扫描宗卷";
"Safety reserve" = "安全保留量";
"Leave free" = "保留的空闲空间";
"Free space kept unwritten so the volume never fills completely (which can crash apps or the OS). A small amount of free space is therefore left un-wiped by design." = "为防止宗卷被完全填满（这可能导致应用或操作系统崩溃），会保留一部分空闲空间不进行写入。因此会有意留下少量未擦除的空闲空间。";
"In progress" = "进行中";
"How this works & its limits" = "工作原理及其局限性";
"Only free space is overwritten. The wipe creates new files in a hidden scratch folder and fills them — the system only ever allocates unused blocks to new files, so your existing data is never read or written." = "仅会覆写空闲空间。擦除操作会在隐藏的临时文件夹中创建新文件并将其填满——系统只会将未使用的块分配给新文件，因此您现有的数据绝不会被读取或写入。";
"Corrupted, orphaned or \"ghost\" data sitting in unallocated blocks is treated as free and overwritten." = "位于未分配块中的损坏、孤立或“幽灵”数据会被视为空闲空间并被覆写。";
"On SSDs (TRIM) and APFS, the platform may already have electronically erased free blocks, and wear-levelling means a logical overwrite isn't guaranteed to hit the same physical cells. This is most effective on HDDs and external/USB drives." = "在 SSD（TRIM）和 APFS 上，平台可能已经以电子方式擦除了空闲块，并且由于损耗均衡，逻辑层面的覆写并不能保证作用于相同的物理单元。此功能在 HDD 以及外接/USB 驱动器上最为有效。";
"APFS snapshots and local Time Machine backups keep old blocks \"in use,\" so data they reference isn't free space and won't be wiped until those snapshots are removed." = "APFS 快照和本地 Time Machine 备份会将旧块保持为“使用中”状态，因此它们所引用的数据并非空闲空间，在这些快照被移除之前不会被擦除。";
"This fills the free space on \"%@\" with %@, then removes the fill files. Your existing files are never touched — only unused space is overwritten. It can take a long time and will make the disk appear full while it runs." = "此操作会用 %@ 填满“%@”上的空闲空间，然后移除填充文件。您现有的文件绝不会被触及——只会覆写未使用的空间。该过程可能耗时较长，并会使磁盘在运行期间看起来已满。";

